From b390ef05826040796c97b9a1c40e5cbc75170fde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: drcano <156254264+drcano@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:45:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] feat(disputes): add provide_dispute_evidence tool

Today's toolkit can list, get and accept disputes but cannot submit
evidence. The new tool reads the dispute first and follows its own
HATEOAS links: provide-evidence when offered, else
provide-supporting-info (some states allow only that, and
provide-evidence returns ACTION_NOT_ALLOWED_IN_CURRENT_DISPUTE_STATE),
failing clearly if neither is offered.

- multipart/form-data with an input JSON part; the JSON Content-Type
  from getHeaders() is dropped so axios does not serialize the form as JSON
- evidence_type limited to the enum in customer_disputes_v1.json
- optional base64 documents attached as file parts

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
